Requirements
Requirement	Module	Access program	Statement
relational-model.1	relational model		The relational model MUST give the access programs of format and query as its own: loads and load, dumps and dump, instances and named, chosen and kept.
format.1	format		format MUST give the access programs of the parser, the generator and JSON text as its own: loads and load, dumps and dump, instances and named.
parser.1	parser		The parser MUST accept every MTSV file that conforms, as MTSV-DRAFT decides for parsers.
parser.2	parser		The parser MUST treat a U+FEFF at the start of the text as an encoding signature, and not as part of the first field.
parser.3	parser		The parser MUST raise not MTSV for text that does not conform, its reason the number of the line where it stops conforming, counted from 1.
parser.4	parser	load	load MUST decode its octets as UTF-8, the character set of an MTSV file whose media type names none, before parsing them.
generator.1	generator		The generator MUST write only MTSV files that conform, as MTSV-DRAFT decides for generators: an FF line before every sheet, the first included, a line break after every record, in UTF-8.
generator.2	generator		The generator MUST raise cannot be represented for a field or sheet name that holds HT, LF, FF or CR, its reason the sheet's position, the record's position and the field's position, joined by a space, the sheet and the field counted from 1, the record 0 for the sheet name, 1 for the header and from 2 for the records.
generator.3	generator	dump	dump MUST encode the MTSV text in UTF-8.
json-text.1	JSON text	instances	JSON text MUST read a JSON text in UTF-8 as RFC 8259 defines it, a byte order mark at its start not ignored.
json-text.8	JSON text	instances	JSON text MUST reject what is not a JSON text as not a JSON text.
json-text.2	JSON text	instances	JSON text MUST give each instance of the text one record of instances, the value itself first and every instance before the instances within it, in the order written, its _parent the instance that holds it and its _pointer the JSON Pointer to it from that instance, ~ in a member name written ~0 and / written ~1.
json-text.3	JSON text	instances	_type MUST be the instance's primitive type, an integer a number, and _value its text: a string's characters, a number as written, true or false, and empty for null, an object and an array.
json-text.4	JSON text	instances	A string that holds FF, a line break or HT MUST have an empty _value, its text written to runs: split at each FF into pages, each page at each LF or CRLF into lines, each line at each HT into runs, a CRLF read as LF.
json-text.5	JSON text	instances	A CR not followed by LF, a character that is not a Unicode character, and HT, LF, FF or CR in a member name within a pointer MUST be left out, each place one is left out given as not carried by its JSON Pointer within the text.
json-text.6	JSON text	instances	An object whose names are not all unique MUST end the read as names not unique, its reason the JSON Pointer to the first object, in the order written, that repeats one, in its URI fragment representation.
json-text.7	JSON text	named	named MUST give the instance a JSON Pointer names among a text's instances, evaluated from the text's value as RFC 6901 evaluates it, each reference token the _pointer of an instance within the one before it, and no instance where the pointer names none.
query.1	query	kept	query MUST give the access program kept of filter expression as its own.
query.2	query	chosen	Selection MUST give restriction by records and filter, projection by fields, join by join, and union by the sheets of one name from several origins.
query.3	query	chosen	chosen MUST take the file each sheet is of from origins, so that sheet and join count and name the sheets of each file, and lead each record of a union by lead, file its file's position and _input its file's source.
query.4	query	chosen	sheets MUST give each sheet chosen of each file: its records, the records of it the filter keeps, and the positions of those named in the sheet it is given in.
query.5	query		A selection, filter or join refused MUST end chosen and kept as refused, with its reason.
positions.1	positions	named	sheet, records and fields MUST each be written as 2, 1;3, 1-3 or 2-*, counting from 1 within what holds it.
positions.4	positions	named	A selection not written as positions.1 writes it MUST be refused.
positions.2	positions	named	Positions that do not exist MUST be left out.
positions.3	positions	written	positions MUST write each run of consecutive positions, a run of one as its position and a longer run as its first and last joined by -, the runs joined by ;, and no position as the empty text.
filter-expression.1	filter expression	kept	filter MUST be a filter expression in which @[0] is a record's first field, and keep the records for which it holds.
filter-expression.2	filter expression	kept	A filter not written as filter-expression.1 writes it MUST be refused.
set-operations.1	set operations	union	The union MUST give each sheet name once, its records those of every sheet of that name in the files or inputs read, in their order, each record led by the file or the _input it came from.
set-operations.2	set operations	union	Sheets of one name whose headers differ MUST be given apart by the union.
operations-on-relations.1	operations on relations	restrict	Restriction MUST keep the records whose positions records names and for which filter holds.
operations-on-relations.3	operations on relations	project	Projection MUST keep the fields whose positions fields names.
operations-on-relations.4	operations on relations	restrict	With a filter, records MUST count the records the filter keeps.
operations-on-relations.2	operations on relations	project	A sheet left with no field MUST come back empty.
operations-on-relations.5	operations on relations	join	join MUST name sheets of each file as sheet does, and give their natural join on every column whose name they share, before records, filter and fields are applied, the sheet it gives named by the names of the sheets joined, in order, joined by *, as a natural join is written.
operations-on-relations.6	operations on relations	join	A join of sheets that share no column MUST be refused.
